<body style="height: auto; min-height: auto;">Ref No: {{{Case.Case_Number__c}}}<br />
<br />
Hi {{{Case.First_Name__c}}}<br />
<br />
<b>RE: {{{Case.Baggage_File_Reference__c}}}</b><br />
<br />
Thank you for getting in touch with the Qantas Customer Care team.<br />
&nbsp;<br />
I'm sorry to hear about your mishandled baggage on your recent flight to {{{Case.Arrival_City__c}}} and this letter is to confirm details of your report.<br />
<br />
<strong>We're here to help</strong>&nbsp;<br />
Our records show that you left {{{Case.Departure_City__c}}} on {{{Case.Email_Departure_Date_Time__c}}}, arriving in {{{Case.Arrival_City__c}}} on {{{Case.Email_Arrival_Date_Time__c}}}, reporting the loss of your baggage.<br />
&nbsp;<br />
<strong>If bag has been found, use:</strong><br />
<br />
Your baggage was located on {{{Case.Located_Date__c}}} and was delivered to you in {{{Case.Delivery_Port__c}}} on {{{Case.Delivery_Date__c}}}.<br />
<br />
<strong>If bag has not been found, use:</strong><br />
&nbsp;<br />
Your baggage has been assessed as lost, and compensation has been provided in line with the applicable liability limits under the Montreal Convention &lt;AUD$0.00&gt; or the Civil Aviation (Carriers’ Liability) Act &lt;AUD$0.00&gt;.<br />
<br />
I hope this information helps you with your insurance claim - please don't hesitate to contact us should you require any further information.<br />
&nbsp;</body>
